WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.511
India buys grain at support prices,

2
00:00:02.611 --> 00:00:04.425
and stores it for food security.

3
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:06.905
Under WTO farm rules, that

4
00:00:06.905 --> 00:00:08.345
support has a cap:

5
00:00:08.495 --> 00:00:10.287
10 percent of the crop's value,

6
00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:13.373
priced at 1986-88 prices.

7
00:00:13.773 --> 00:00:15.640
Cross it, and India could

8
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.059
face a WTO dispute.

9
00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:19.129
Unless the peace clause applies.

10
00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:21.613
Agreed at Bali in 2013,

11
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.536
and extended in 2014 until

12
00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:25.616
a permanent solution is found,

13
00:00:25.736 --> 00:00:27.637
it stops members from challenging

14
00:00:27.637 --> 00:00:29.019
staple-crop stockholding

15
00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:29.768
in a dispute.

16
00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:32.048
India first invoked it in

17
00:00:32.048 --> 00:00:33.176
2020, for rice,

18
00:00:33.296 --> 00:00:35.003
and has invoked it again since.

19
00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:37.579
But there is still no permanent solution,

20
00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:40.080
not even at the WTO's March

21
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.285
2026 ministerial meeting.

22
00:00:42.735 --> 00:00:43.631
A shield,

23
00:00:43.781 --> 00:00:45.040
not a settlement.

24
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.436
Your turn.

25
00:00:46.736 --> 00:00:48.443
What does the peace clause protect?
